Pin offline-replay requests to specific workers in Dynamo's Mocker (KV router mode).

DYN_REPLAY_PINS names a JSON file {"aggregated": {request_id: worker}, "prefill": {...}, "decode": {...}};
the KV router then places each listed request on that worker instead of selecting one. Request IDs come
from agentic-format traces (Mooncake rows have none). pd_packing.run_mocker_pd writes the file.

Against ai-dynamo de80aabb58a96a0424b68ce9d1b83b7c59552800 (the requirements.txt pin). To build:
    git clone https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo && cd dynamo && git checkout de80aabb58a96a0424b68ce9d1b83b7c59552800
    git apply /path/to/soldr/patches/dynamo-replay-pins.patch
    cd lib/bindings/python && uvx --from 'maturin>=1.0,<2.0' maturin build --release --features ais-forward-pass \
        -i /path/to/soldr/.venv/bin/python -o dist
    uv pip install --python /path/to/soldr/.venv/bin/python --no-deps --reinstall dist/ai_dynamo_runtime-*.whl

